From 6f59fda4496d9a7b0c4c2b9fc32d107133fedf39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarkPronkin <109197080+MarkPronkin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:58:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: Support passive Intel profiles on MacBookPro8,2

---
 README.md                 |  18 ++++++
 src/ppd-driver-cpufreq.c  | 131 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/integration_test.py |  95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 243 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index bc7b8f7..df9c9c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -308,6 +308,24 @@ next profile change or resume, which caps it like the others. A cluster that is
 offline when the daemon stops can't have its cap lifted, and keeps it until it
 is written again or the system restarts.
 
+### Passive Intel P-State on the 2011 15-inch MacBook Pro
+
+On `MacBookPro8,2`, the cpufreq driver also handles passive `intel_cpufreq`
+when no energy-performance preference is available. The existing Intel
+P-State driver still takes priority when it can use EPP or EPB. All other
+Intel models keep their current driver.
+
+The tested i7-2760QM uses `schedutil` in all three profiles to avoid pinning
+this 45 W CPU at maximum frequency. Performance raises the floor to 1.2 GHz;
+balanced uses the hardware minimum and maximum. Power-saver restores the
+hardware minimum, caps the maximum at 1.8 GHz and disables turbo. Limits are
+clamped to each policy's hardware range. No frequency table is required.
+
+Profiles are reapplied after resume and include policies that have become
+available since startup. Stopping the daemon restores balanced settings.
+The standard daemon owns D-Bus, authorization, holds and profile persistence;
+no separate service is needed.
+
 ## Multiple driver and multiple action operations
 
 Power-profiles daemon will load all supported drivers and actions by default.
diff --git a/src/ppd-driver-cpufreq.c b/src/ppd-driver-cpufreq.c
index 3940c73..cc29b0e 100644
--- a/src/ppd-driver-cpufreq.c
+++ b/src/ppd-driver-cpufreq.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
